  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\left[a_{i j}\\right]$ be a square matrix of order 2 with entries either 0 or 1 . Let $E$ be the event that $A$ is an invertible matrix. Then the probability $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{E})$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "RIrdC",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{16}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FwPd9",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hjhOY",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HooGE",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A=\\left[a_y\\right]_{2 \\times 2}$ and entries are 0 or 1.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore\\left|\\begin{array}{ll}\na & b \\\\\nc & d\n\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow a d-b c=0\n\\end{aligned}$\nCase I: $a d=b c=1$\n$\\therefore \\quad a=b=c=d=1$\nCase II: $a d=b c=0$\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\na=0, d=0 & b=0, c=0 \\\\\na=0, d=1 & b=0, c=1 \\\\\na=1, d=0 & b=1, c=0\n\\end{array}$\n$\\therefore$ Total 10 cases when matrix is non invertible Total possible matrix $=2^4=16$\nRequired probability of invertible\n$=\\frac{16-10}{16}=\\frac{6}{16}=\\frac{3}{8}$",
    "image": null
  },
